    "interpretation": "Negative binding energy in an Nf>=2 sector reproduces the paper's core ED result that flipped spins bind into a many-magnon droplet (the quantum skyrmion). Nonzero scalar chirality in that sector signals the topological (skyrmion-like) texture. FM wins the GLOBAL ground state at these fields; the skyrmion is a bound state within a fixed-magnetization sector, exactly as the paper frames it (stability vs quantum evaporation, Eq.4).",
